# Project Guidelines

## 1. Dual-Theme Parity (Light & Dark Mode Mandatory)
- **Every new feature, screen, drawer, modal, table, card, and UI element MUST be designed and developed to support BOTH Light Mode and Dark Mode with equal visual quality.**
- **Never develop for Dark Mode only.** When creating or updating UI, always ensure high-contrast readability, balanced contrast ratios, and clean aesthetics in Light Mode as well as Dark Mode.
- **Use Semantic Design Tokens**:
  - Backgrounds: `bg-background`, `bg-card`, `bg-surface`, `bg-surface-elevated`, `bg-surface-hover`, `bg-secondary`, `bg-muted` or `var(--bg-primary)`, `var(--surface)`, etc.
  - Text: `text-foreground`, `text-muted-foreground`, `text-text-primary`, `text-text-secondary`, `text-text-muted`, `text-text-disabled`.
  - Borders: `border-border`, `border-border-default`, `border-border-strong`, `border-border-subtle`, `border-input`.
  - Accents: `bg-primary`, `text-primary-foreground`, `bg-accent`, `text-accent-foreground`.
- **Avoid One-Sided Glassmorphic/Opacity Hacks**:
  - Never hardcode dark-mode-only alpha utilities like `bg-white/5` or `border-white/10` without corresponding light/dark classes or semantic variables. In light mode, `border-white/10` and `bg-white/5` are invisible or produce illegible contrast.
  - If using glassmorphic surfaces, pair them properly: `bg-white/85 dark:bg-zinc-900/80 border border-zinc-200 dark:border-white/10 backdrop-blur-xl` or use semantic glass classes like `aether-glass` with dynamic variable bindings.
  - Never use static `text-white` on transparent surfaces that will be rendered on a light background.

## 2. UI Anti-Patterns & Clean Aesthetics
- **No Decorative AI Slop**: Never use pill badges, next-gen labels, or decorative tags (such as `inline-flex items-center gap-2 ... rounded-full`) with Sparkles/icons at the top of landing page sections, hero sections, feature pages, or anywhere else in the project. Ensure this type of div is never used anytime anywhere.
- **No Floating Hero Micro-Widgets**: Never use floating micro-widgets (such as absolute positioned glass divs with `absolute -bottom-6 -left-6` or `-right-6` showing status or metadata like "Active Workspace Operations Board", "Workspace Authority", etc.) next to the main hero screenshots in the feature pages. Keep screenshot and graphic presentations clean.
